## Build-time dependencies

These are installed by the container, not vendored into this repository, and keep
their own licenses: ROS 2 Jazzy, MoveIt 2, `ros2_control`, Gazebo Harmonic, `ros_gz`,
OpenCV, and BehaviorTree.CPP with BehaviorTree.ROS2 (built from
`.docker/underlay.repos` into `/opt/underlay`).

## Why `sorting_arm_description/package.xml` says MIT

That manifest, and everything in the package outside the paths listed above (the
launch wiring, the sorting-cell-specific xacro layers, and the configuration), is
MIT-licensed original work. The vendored UR5e and Robotiq 2F-85 files remain
BSD-3-Clause regardless of what the manifest declares; this file is the license
record for them.
